                     /note="cyanorak cluster number:CK_00008054"
                     /note="cyanorak V1 cluster number:8054"
                     /note="60 kDa chaperone family; promotes refolding of misf
                     olded polypeptides especially under stressful conditions; 
                     forms two stacked rings of heptamers to form a barrel-shap
                     ed 14mer; ends can be capped by GroES; misfolded proteins 
                     enter the barrel where they are refolded when GroES binds;
                      many bacteria have multiple copies of the groEL gene whic
                     h are active under different environmental conditions; the
                      B.japonicum protein in this cluster is expressed constitu
                     tively; in Rhodobacter, Corynebacterium and Rhizobium this
                      protein is essential for growth"
                     /transl_table="11"
                     /codon_start="1"
                     /db_xref="GeneID:5730378"
