                     /note="cyanorak cluster number:CK_00000508"
                     /note="cyanorak V1 cluster number:508"
                     /note="RpmE; there appears to be two types of ribosomal pr
                     oteins L31 in bacterial genomes; some contain a CxxC motif
                      while others do not; Bacillus subtilis has both types; th
                     e proteins in this cluster do not have the CXXC motif; Rpm
                     E is found in exponentially growing Bacilli while YtiA was
                      found after exponential growth; expression of ytiA is con
                     trolled by a zinc-specific transcriptional repressor; RpmE
                      contains one zinc ion and a CxxC motif is responsible for
                      this binding; forms an RNP particle along with proteins L
                     5, L18, and L25 and 5S rRNA; found crosslinked to L2 and L
                     25 and EF-G; may be near the peptidyltransferase site of t
                     he 50S ribosome"
