                     /note="cyanorak cluster number:CK_00000120"
                     /note="cyanorak V1 cluster number:120"
                     /note="functions in protein export; can interact with acid
                     ic membrane phospholipids and the SecYEG protein complex; 
                     binds to preproteins; binds to ATP and undergoes a conform
                     ational change to promote membrane insertion of SecA/bound
                      preprotein; ATP hydrolysis appears to drive release of th
                     e preprotein from SecA and deinsertion of SecA from the me
                     mbrane; additional proteins SecD/F/YajC aid SecA recycling
                     ; exists in an equilibrium between monomers and dimers; ma
                     y possibly form higher order oligomers; in some organisms,
                      there are paralogous proteins that have been found to be 
                     nonessential but do function in secretion of a subset of e
                     xported proteins"
                     /codon_start="1"
