                     /note="cyanorak V1 cluster number:314"
                     /note="RibE; 6,7-diimethyl-8-ribityllumazine synthase; DMR
                     L synthase; lumazine synthase; beta subunit of riboflavin 
                     synthase; condenses 5-amino-6-(1'-D)-ribityl-amino-2,4(1H,
                     3H)-pyrimidinedione with L-3,4-dihydrohy-2-butanone-4-phos
                     phate to generate 6,6-dimethyl-8-lumazine (DMRL); riboflav
                     in synthase then uses 2 molecules of DMRL to produce ribof
                     lavin (vitamin B12); involved in the last steps of ribofla
                     vin biosynthesis; forms a 60mer (icosahedral shell) in bot
                     h Bacillus subtilis and Escherichia coli; in Bacillus subt
                     ilis this 60mer is associated with the riboflavin synthase
                      subunit (alpha) while in Escherichia coli it is not"
